    <node id="DOC_ep_2026-03-26_item003.txt_S9">
      <data key="d0">SEGMENT</data>
      <data key="d1">lexical_graph</data>
      <data key="d4">Kathleen | Van Brempt: Do I have to remind us that, this year alone – and we are only in March – the US threatened to invade Greenland, coerced Spain, breached – once again – the deal with new tariffs and, just this week, threatened to raise energy prices for Europe in the wake of an illegal war that they started and which has already spiked prices globally? ' That is exactly why we say today: no free pass, no blank check. We do not approve the deal today. We vote for a strong Parliament position, which has been clearly outlined by our rapporteur, Bernd Lange, with clear guarantees. We will only act once the US honours its commitments, including bringing the tariffs on steel down, so that Europe can respond when these commitments are broken and so that our industry is protected against new chaos. That is why we support this mandate today, because it draws clear conditions and gives Europe the tools to suspend, to react and to protect itself. But let there be no misunderstanding, and I address our Commission – there will be no final approval by our group if these conditions are not fully met. Colleagues, to conclude, we will not be intimidated. We will not be bullied into a bad deal. Today, we show our citizens that this European Parliament stands up for their interest and for our Europe. I urge the Council and the Commission to finally show some courage and do the same.</data>
      <data key="d5">16</data>
      <data key="d2">Kathleen | Van Bremp...</data>
      <data key="d6">{}</data>
    </node>
